it came close to saturation

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:44.000
so this is pretty much the journey of this data set

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:47.000
if you read about its tasks and data set details

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:50.000
then as I said expert level questions

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:53.000
in biology, physics and chemistry

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:56.000
a typical question looks like this

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:59.000
physics question I guess

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:02.000
particle spin etc. has been discussed

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:05.000
there are 4 options and you have to select the best option

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:08.000
as you can see in most of the knowledge benchmarks

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:11.000
here I have told you that there are 3 subsets

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:14.000
in this entire benchmark, main, extended and diamond

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:17.000
and the task is that you will be given only 4 options

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:20.000
you have to tell the correct answer in one question

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:23.000
and the metric is accuracy obviously

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:26.000
run configuration is the same

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:29.000
zero shot, chain of thought allowed, temperature 0

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:32.000
pass at the rate 1 and tools access is not given

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:35.000
and if we discuss 2 important pointers

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:38.000
that what does this data set not measure

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:41.000
so first of all it does not measure

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:44.000
general graduate knowledge

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:47.000
till now our data sets were targeting

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:50.000
general knowledge, this is strictly

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:53.000
the target benchmark of science

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:56.000
so if a model is scoring very hard

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:59.000
then it is only a representation of this

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.000
that that model has absorbed the knowledge

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:05.000
of science very well, the rest is not guaranteed

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:08.000
second open-ended problem solving

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:11.000
this benchmark does not tell you anything

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:14.000
here you are simply selecting one option from the given options

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:17.000
it does not mean that when it will be given an open-ended

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:20.000
question of science then it will give you good results

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:23.000
and lastly here

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:26.000
the reasoning trace is not being evaluated

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:29.000
you may know what reasoning models do

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:32.000
reasoning models internally reason

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:35.000
before giving any answer

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:38.000
so we give them a task pad

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:41.000
and we also give them a token budget

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:44.000
that look we have a token budget, you can think in this much

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:47.000
so internally they think, you may have seen

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:50.000
while using chart GPT, it is written there

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:53.000
that now the model is doing this, now this, now this, we call it reasoning

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:56.000
so the reasoning trace

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:59.000
we are not evaluating it, which basically means

00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:02.000
that we are not evaluating this thing that how the model

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:05.000
is reaching the answer, there are many ways to reach the answer

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:08.000
you are directly calculating the right answer

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:11.000
or you are eliminating the wrong options

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:14.000
or you are putting a mark on it

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:17.000
anything can happen, right?

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:20.000
so here we are not validating the correctness of reasoning trace

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:23.000
which basically means that if the model is putting a mark internally

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:26.000
and it is correct then we are giving it marks

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:29.000
so this benchmark does not measure these three things

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:32.000
if we discuss some known issues

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:35.000
or criticisms

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:38.000
then the biggest criticism is that there are very few questions

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:41.000
in comparison to past data sets where we have seen

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:44.000
14000-15000 questions

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:47.000
here there are only 198 questions

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:50.000
so the more the questions decrease

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:53.000
the less your confidence on the result decreases

00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:56.000
you had read this in statistics especially in hypothesis testing

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:59.000
so your confidence interval rating is not very

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:02.000
