where you will read about multi benchmark leaderboards

01:24:17.000 --> 01:24:20.000
from the name it is clear that these are such leaderboards

01:24:20.000 --> 01:24:23.000
which together

01:24:23.000 --> 01:24:26.000
bring the results of multiple benchmarks

01:24:26.000 --> 01:24:29.000
and give a cumulative score

01:24:29.000 --> 01:24:32.000
so it is written here

01:24:32.000 --> 01:24:35.000
these leaderboards compare models across multiple benchmarks

01:24:35.000 --> 01:24:38.000
and evaluation dimensions instead of relying on just one test

01:24:38.000 --> 01:24:41.000
so it is possible that a leaderboard

01:24:41.000 --> 01:24:44.000
which combines knowledge, reasoning, mathematics

01:24:44.000 --> 01:24:47.000
coding, instruction following, data analysis

01:24:47.000 --> 01:24:50.000
and makes a leaderboard by combining these benchmarks

01:24:50.000 --> 01:24:53.000
I will show you an example

01:24:53.000 --> 01:24:56.000
a good example of this is livebench

01:24:56.000 --> 01:24:59.000
see it is written here

01:24:59.000 --> 01:25:02.000
a challenging contamination free LLM benchmark

01:25:02.000 --> 01:25:05.000
which has 23 objective tasks across 7 categories

01:25:05.000 --> 01:25:08.000
reasoning, coding, agentic coding

01:25:08.000 --> 01:25:11.000
how much score is there in every model

01:25:11.000 --> 01:25:14.000
and an overall score is also shown

01:25:14.000 --> 01:25:17.000
this is like a more useful leaderboard

01:25:17.000 --> 01:25:20.000
because it gives you an overall view

01:25:20.000 --> 01:25:23.000
of how a model is in general in multiple capabilities

